<!--
  Pidgin English Camerounais (Kamtok / PCM / WES) — v2.1.52
  Couverture complete 206/206.

  Source : connaissances Kamtok (creole anglais simplifie tres parle au Cameroun,
  surtout regions Nord-Ouest, Sud-Ouest, et urbain Douala/Yaounde).
  + Wikipedia "Cameroonian Pidgin English" pour la grammaire de base.

  Notes Kamtok :
  - "di" = progressive aspect (-ing)
  - "don/dong" = perfect aspect (have done)
  - "go" = future
  - "fit" = can/be able to
  - "wan/wanti" = want
  - "sabi" = know
  - "tchop" = eat
  - "waka" = walk/function
  - "no" = not (negation)
  - "dem" = plural marker / they
  - "sef" = self/emphasis
  - "sharp sharp" = quickly, urgently
  - "small small" = slowly, little by little

  Marqueurs medicaux Kamtok :
  - "sugar sickness" = diabete
  - "sugar level" = glycemie
  - "white pesin" = medecin (lit. "personne blanche", historique)
  - "hospital" = hopital (anglais conserve)
  - "doctor" = medecin
  - "medicine" = medicament
  - "i di pain me" = j'ai mal
  - "ma body weak" = je suis faible
  - "ma belly di pain" = j'ai mal au ventre

  AVERTISSEMENT : traductions de mes meilleurs efforts. Avant production
  grande echelle, demander une review a un native speaker camerounais.
-->
